<section class="content-section">
    <div class="container faq-columns">
        <section class="faq-list" aria-labelledby="reiki-faq-heading">
            <h2 id="reiki-faq-heading">Reiki</h2>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>What is Reiki?</h3>
                <p>Reiki is a gentle, hands-on (or near-body) energy healing practice that helps calm the nervous system, release tension, and support the body's natural ability to restore balance.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>What happens during a session?</h3>
                <p>You'll relax fully clothed on a treatment table while I use light touch or hands slightly above the body to channel energy. Most people feel warmth, gentle tingling, or deep relaxation.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>Is Reiki right for me if I'm skeptical?</h3>
                <p>Absolutely. Reiki is a deeply relaxing experience on its own, and you don't need to believe in anything specific for it to be beneficial. Come as you are, curious or not.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>How many sessions will I need?</h3>
                <p>Every person is different. Some feel significant shifts after one session, while others prefer ongoing sessions for deeper, lasting support. We can talk through what feels right for you.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>What should I do to prepare?</h3>
                <p>Wear comfortable clothing, avoid a heavy meal right beforehand, and come with an open mind. There's nothing else you need to do &mdash; just arrive as you are.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>Do you offer distance Reiki?</h3>
                <p>Yes. Energy healing isn't limited by physical distance, so I offer remote sessions for clients who aren't local or who simply prefer to receive a session at home.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>What is your cancellation policy?</h3>
                <p>I ask for at least 24 hours' notice to reschedule or cancel a session so that I can offer the time to another client.</p>
            </div>
        </section>
        <section class="faq-list" aria-labelledby="dbb-faq-heading">
            <h2 id="dbb-faq-heading">Dynamic Body Balancing</h2>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>What is Dynamic Body Balancing?</h3>
                <p>Dynamic Body Balancing (DBB) is a gentle bodywork approach that combines fascial release, craniosacral techniques, and energy-based practices to support relaxation, body awareness, and a sense of balance. <a href="services/body-balancing">Learn more about Dynamic Body Balancing.</a></p>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>What happens during a session?</h3>
                <p>You remain fully clothed and may sit, stand, or lie down. We use gentle touch and guided movement while inviting you to notice your body's responses. Your body leads the movement, and we support you at your own pace, with attention to your comfort and boundaries.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>Is Dynamic Body Balancing right for me?</h3>
                <p>You may be interested in DBB if you'd like to slow down, become more aware of tension, or explore gentle movement and body awareness. You don't need prior experience or a particular belief to begin. DBB is a complementary wellness practice, not a substitute for medical evaluation, diagnosis, or treatment.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>How many sessions will I need?</h3>
                <p>There is no set number that fits everyone. Your experience and reasons for seeking a session are individual. We can talk through what you're looking for and revisit whether you'd like another session based on your comfort and experience.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>What should I do to prepare?</h3>
                <p>Wear comfortable clothing that allows you to move easily. Before we begin, let us know about any movement limitations or preferences around touch so we can keep your comfort and boundaries central to the session.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>Will I need to move during a session?</h3>
                <p>We may invite you to notice and follow gentle, intuitive movement rather than a prescribed sequence. Experiences vary: you may notice relaxation, changes in body awareness, or emotional responses. There is no right or wrong way to respond, and you are encouraged to move at your own pace.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>What is your cancellation policy?</h3>
                <p>We ask for at least 24 hours' notice to reschedule or cancel a session so that we can offer the time to another client.</p>
            </div>
        </section>
    </div>
</section>

